Text:
The manager GUI is a program written in Fearless, part of the standard library.
The 'manager window' is the window of the manager GUI.
The manager GUI sends each request of the user to the 'single' manager with fearlessMessage.
fearlessManager tells the manager GUI the News, on the standard input of the manager GUI.

Grammar:
News ::= Told1 .. Toldn
Told ::= Message, " Applied\n" | Message, " Refused\n"

Define ManagerGui$start:
A fearlessManager runs the manager GUI in a process of its own, and writes on the standard input of the manager GUI.
B The manager GUI reads projects.info.
C The manager GUI applies each Told of the News, in the order fearlessManager tells them.

Define managerGui$send(m):
A The manager GUI runs fearlessMessage m.
B fearlessMessage prints the Answer Applied.

Define managerGui$send(m):
A The manager GUI runs fearlessMessage m.
B fearlessMessage prints the Answer Refused, with the Error e.
C The manager GUI shows e in a dialog of the 'manager window'.

Story:
A fearlessManager tells the manager GUI Show Applied.
B The manager GUI shows the 'manager window'.
C The manager GUI asks the desk to bring the 'manager window' to the front.

Story:
A The user closes the 'manager window'.
B The manager GUI ends.

Story:
A The standard input of the manager GUI ends.
B The manager GUI ends.
